  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the main uncertainty is whether a simple RNA-only representation provides a useful performance baseline before adding multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders, image features, or fusion. config_001 tests the simplest RNA-only single-profile PCA model, isolating the effect of basic RNA representation without confounding changes to profile setting, aggregation, or fusion. It is the best first use of a limited budget because it is low-complexity, cheap to interpret, and establishes an anchor for later comparisons against multiprofile, alternative RNA encoders, image-only, and multimodal configurations."
}

